  "answer": "The ticket has no details, so this is a best match on the symptom: the Text Extractor shortcut does nothing. Past tickets point to three things to check. (1) Another program may be taking the hotkey. In #27893 a third-party app (BijoyBanno) blocked all PowerToys shortcuts. Closing or disabling other keyboard or input utilities fixed it, and you can also set a different Text Extractor shortcut. (2) The OCR language pack may be missing. In #33242 the maintainers asked for the output of `Get-WindowsCapability -Online | Where-Object { $_.Name -Like 'Language.OCR*' }` in PowerShell. Your system language is Chinese (Hong Kong), so check that zh-HK or zh-CN OCR is installed under Settings > Time & language > Language & region. That ticket had no confirmed fix. (3) #45911 reported the same symptom, where the capture overlay never appears after the hotkey. It was closed as a duplicate of #33242, which is still unresolved. If none of this helps, update PowerToys, restart it, and file a new ticket with the shortcut you use, the steps to reproduce, and a Report Bug zip."
